            {"id": "b", "text": "RAM — total VM memory allocation plus host OS overhead will exhaust the 64 GB physical RAM as additional VMs are added", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. Current allocation: 3 VMs × 12 GB = 36 GB + ~8 GB host OS overhead = ~44 GB used of 64 GB. A fourth VM adds 12 GB (56 GB total), leaving only ~8 GB for host overhead — tight. A fifth VM would push total demand past 64 GB, triggering pagefile swapping and severe performance degradation. RAM is the first hard limit in this configuration."},
